  "id": "SprySOCKS_Windows_Variant_Abuses_Kernel_Drivers_to_Evade_Detection_txt_9",
  "content": "Specifically, WIN_DRV uses two encrypted kernel drivers, the first of which is fsdiskbit.sys or, as ESET researchers call it, \"DriverLoader.\" The aptly named driver is delivered via the SprySOCKS loader and serves a single purpose: to load the second kernel driver, named \"RawWNPF,\" directly into the memory of the target system.",
